illumos (process.platform 'sunos'): the desktop editor takes the Linux branches
in its startup (src/mainImpl.ts, src/bootstrap-node.ts) and the update service
(electron-main/app.ts), as FreeBSD's editors/vscode does for 'freebsd'
(https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-ports/tree/main/editors/vscode/files).
The build takes our Electron (developer/electron-43) from the download cache,
so the release checksums are off (build/lib/electron.ts, as FreeBSD).
The launcher checks /proc/version (WSL) only where it exists, and exports
IBUS_ENABLE_SYNC_MODE=1 (ibus-gtk3's async mode loses the keys on illumos).

--- a/build/lib/electron.ts	2026-11-18 08:33:07.070282949 +0100
+++ b/build/lib/electron.ts	2026-11-18 08:33:07.070282949 +0100
@@ -240,7 +240,10 @@
 	winIcon: 'resources/win32/code.ico',
 	token: process.env['GITHUB_TOKEN'],
 	repo: electronAssetResolver,
-	validateChecksum: true,
+	// Our own Electron build (developer/electron-43) stands in for the
+	// download: its checksums are not the release's.
+	validateChecksum: false,
+	unsafelyDisableChecksums: true,
 	checksumFile: path.join(root, 'build', 'checksums', 'electron.txt'),
 	createVersionedResources: useVersionedUpdate,
 	productVersionString: versionedResourcesFolder,
--- a/src/bootstrap-node.ts	2026-11-18 08:33:07.062282938 +0100
